      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name}\n\nHere's the test avatar I made: avtr_355bf6f1-325c-4955-9843-0d8b8c620dd8\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n1. Equip the avatar similar to what explained in the issue.\n\n2. Enter the AFK State.\n\n3. Wait until the character disappears.\n\n4. Try to leave the AFK State.\n\nAfter doing that, you'll see that you can move again and the AFK icon in the HUD is gone as well. However the character will not appear again. If you check Avatar Debug, you'll see that the AFK parameter is stuck at \"true\".\n\nI also tested it in Unity 2022.3.22f1 using Gesture Manager Emulator and the issue is not present there.",
