      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "Thanks for your report. What you're describing is expected behavior because an avatar's animator is culled (stops running) for as long as the avatar isn't visible to the local user. Once the avatar becomes visible again, the animator continues and all pending parameter updates (including AFK in your case) are applied.\n\nThis rule applies both when all renderers are disabled (either by the avatar itself or by other means like distance hiding) and when someone fully looks away from you. This is done to boost VRChat's performance, so unfortunately it's unlikely this behavior will change.\n\nNative UI elements showing you're AFK are still updating because those aren't running through your avatar's animator.\n\nYou'll need to update your avatar so it does not have all of its renderers hidden when it goes AFK. In the meantime, we are investigating alternative ways of allowing you to get the behavior you're looking for.\n\nPlease also note that while Gesture Manager is curated by us, it is not an official tool so may not always exactly represent what happens in VRChat itself.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
